    "notes": "1. Total revenue is mapped directly from the 'Revenue' line. 2. Total operating cost is constructed by summing all operating expenses that reduce gross margin to arrive at operating profit. This includes: Cost of sales, Marketing and selling expenses, General and administrative expenses, and Other operating income and expenses (which is a net expense). 'Income/(Loss) from joint ventures and associates' is not included as it is a non-operating item. 3. Net income is mapped to 'Net profit, Group share'. 4. Taxes is mapped directly from 'Income taxes'. 5. Interest expenses includes 'Cost of net financial debt' and 'Interest on lease liabilities' as per standard classification. 'Other financial income and expenses' is not included as it contains non-interest items like dividends, FX, and fair value adjustments. 6. All numbers from the statement are in EUR millions, so scale is 1E6. 7. Parentheses in the source indicate negative values; for expense fields (total_operating_cost, taxes, interest_expenses), these negative values are converted to positive numbers as per the sign convention rule (expenses that reduce income are positive).",
